{{also|Bandit|bändit}}
==English==

===Etymology===
Borrowed from {{bor|en|it|bandito|gloss=outlawed}}, from {{etyl|LL.|en}} {{m|la|bannire||to proclaim}}.<ref>Funk, W. J., ''Word origins and their romantic stories'', New York, Wilfred Funk, Inc.</ref>

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈbændɪt/|lang=en}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# One who [[rob]]s others in a [[lawless]] area, especially as part of a [[group]].
# An [[outlaw]].
# One who [[cheat]]s others.
# {{lb|en|military}} An [[enemy]] [[aircraft]].
# {{lb|en|sports|slang}} A [[runner]] who covertly joins a [[race]] without having [[register]]ed as a [[participant]].

